     "On T1 and T2 the artery is a round signal void (flow void) because of fast flow: the siphon is easiest to find on axial slices lateral to the sella, and the supraclinoid segment just anterolateral to the optic chiasm. On CT angiography and time-of-flight MRA the vessel is bright, and the siphon calcifies with age on non-contrast CT.",
