 location="Originates from the supraclinoid internal carotid immediately after the artery pierces the dural roof of the cavernous sinus, medial to the anterior clinoid process. It runs anteriorly through the optic canal inferolateral to the optic nerve, crosses over the nerve inside the orbit and ends as supratrochlear and dorsal nasal branches at the medial orbital margin.",
