 location="From the carotid terminus at the medial end of the lateral sulcus the A1 (precommunicating) segment passes over the optic nerve or chiasm to the anterior communicating artery; the A2 segment ascends in front of the lamina terminalis and genu of the corpus callosum, and the pericallosal artery (A3 onward) runs back in the callosal sulcus giving off callosomarginal and frontopolar branches.",
 subdivisions=[("A1 (precommunicating)", "gives medial lenticulostriate perforators and the recurrent artery of Heubner near the AComm"), ("A2 (postcommunicating)", "ascends around the genu; orbitofrontal and frontopolar branches"), ("Pericallosal and callosomarginal arteries", "medial frontal and paracentral lobule, precuneus")],
 function="Supplies the paracentral lobule (motor and sensory cortex of the contralateral leg and foot), the medial prefrontal cortex and supplementary motor area, the anterior cingulate, the anterior four-fifths of the corpus callosum, and via Heubner's artery the head of the caudate and anterior limb of the internal capsule.",
